Thank you for your detailed response. I appreciate the authors' effort in improving the paper. Nevertheless, given our previous discussion, I still feel the story of this paper is a bit too biased towards DICE. More specifically:

1) The current title still imply the proposed method is a DICE method;

2) since the work is not based on Eq. (4) or occupancy derivation (currently, there is no word "DICE" appearing in Sec. 4-6), presenting (4) seems unnecessary in the preliminary section, despite that it is a line of related work.
